cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "mechsim: a deterministic limit-order-book simulator for frozen two-mechanism allocation comparison"
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Pathak
    given-names: Manjeet
repository-code: "https://github.com/IIITManjeet/FinanceMeta-Global"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-19"
keywords:
  - market microstructure
  - limit order book
  - price-time priority
  - pro-rata allocation
  - reproducible research
abstract: >-
  A deterministic discrete-event limit order book simulator built to compare
  exactly two allocation mechanisms, price-time priority and pro-rata, under an
  identical state-independent synthetic order-flow realization and a frozen
  latency model. The order-flow generator is independent of book state so that
  both mechanism arms provably consume a byte-identical event stream, making the
  identity control verifiable by hash rather than asserted. Synthetic simulation
  only; it establishes no real-market performance, realized return, predictive
  alpha, market-quality superiority or exchange deployability.
